// Background freeing (opt-in: memorySetBackgroundFree). A collection hands the blocks
// it found unreachable to a helper thread, which free()s them while the program goes
// on; the next collection waits for it first. The helper is the runtime's own (a plain
// pthread, not an Abla thread: collections go on while it runs), and touches nothing
// but those blocks, which nothing can reach. A forked child has no such thread: it
// drops the batch its parent was freeing. A program that doesn't opt in is built with
// the collection above and none of this (nor its state: no global of its own).

// The helper's state, static storage only a program that opts in has: +0 on (0/1),
// +8 the helper's pthread_t, +16 a helper is freeing (0/1), +24 the process that
// started it, +32 the batch the sweep is filling (chunks of [next chunk, count,
// headers…], 65534 headers a chunk).
